/tmp/paper2410.WlagNx/SparseShift.tex:171:\paragraph{Proof sketch.} Like in Section \ref{Subsection: gap reduction}, for a $\CNF$ $\psi$, we carefully analyze the sparsity of the corresponding polynomial $f$ as defined in Section \ref{section-sparseshiftNPH}. For unsatisfiable $\psi$'s, we do a slightly deeper analysis on $\cal S(f(\vecz + \vecb))$, for all $\vecb \in \F^{|\vecz|}$, to show a lower bound. For satisfiable $\psi$'s, $\cal S(f(\vecz + \vecb))$ has already been upper bounded for an appropriate $\vecb \in \F^{|\vecz|}$. The degree parameters are also chosen differently so that the gap between the lower bound and the upper bound is significant. Comparing the sparsities for satisfiable and unsatisfiable $\psi$'s proves part two of Theorem \ref{Theorem: ETSparse_shift NP-hard}. Throughout this section, we assume $\epsilon \in (0,\frac{1}{3})$ to be an arbitrary constant.
